nodes.body:
@zhuzilin could you take a look when you have a moment?

With `--rollout-external-engine-addrs`, slime registers each engine on every run but leaves it registered at shutdown, because the external cluster owns it. A router whose `POST /workers` is create-only then answers the next run with `409 WORKER_ALREADY_EXISTS`, and the run aborts before its first rollout. This change keeps the router's registration when it matches what slime would post. It is the registering counterpart of `unregister_worker` in `server_control.py`. Any other refusal still raises.

The CPU tests are in `tests/test_server_control.py`, and the GPU repro (stock slime fails, patched slime trains) is in the description. Thanks!

